1. [x] Support generate union types from typings [For core devs].

If you write `fillStyle: string | CanvasGradient | null;` at typings, the code generator will auto generate the union C++ class for you.

```c++
class QJSUnionDomStringCanvasGradient final : public UnionBase {
 public:
  using ImplType = std::shared_ptr<QJSUnionDomStringCanvasGradient>;
 ....
};
```

Then you can read the dynamic values from this union class in your C++  code without concerned of the JavaScript types.

```c++
void CanvasRenderingContext2D::setFillStyle(const std::shared_ptr<QJSUnionDomStringCanvasGradient>& style, ExceptionState& exception_state) {
  NativeValue value = Native_NewNull();

  if (style->IsDomString()) {
    value = NativeValueConverter<NativeTypeString>::ToNativeValue(style->GetAsDomString());
  } else if (style->IsCanvasGradient()) {
    value = NativeValueConverter<NativeTypePointer<CanvasGradient>>::ToNativeValue(style->GetAsCanvasGradient());
  }

  //....
}
```

